---
// Fig. for "Coding Theory": turning a message into a low-degree
// polynomial and sending its evaluations — the Reed–Solomon codeword for
// (3, 5) over F(13) at x = 0..4.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 380" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Reed&#8211;Solomon: a message as a line</text>

  <rect x="40" y="46" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">How do we create extra numbers that are all tied to the message?</text>

  <text x="380" y="122" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">MESSAGE&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700">(3, 5) &#8594; the polynomial f(x) = 3 + 5x</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="154" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">EVALUATE&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13" font-weight="700">in F(13) at x = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4</tspan>
  </text>
  <text x="380" y="180" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">f(0)=3, f(1)=8, f(2)=13=0, f(3)=18=5, f(4)=23=10</text>

  <text x="380" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">CODEWORD&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="14" font-weight="700">(3, 8, 0, 5, 10)</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="246" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">SIZES&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13" font-weight="700">k = 2 message numbers, n = 5 sent numbers, rate k/n = 2/5</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="278" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11" font-weight="700">WHY IT WORKS&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#8fdcff" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700">any 2 points determine a line, so any 2 of the 5 numbers recover the message</tspan>
  </text>

  <line x1="40" y1="308" x2="720" y2="308" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="332" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">POINTS OF ONE LOW-DEGREE POLYNOMIAL ARE ALL TIED TOGETHER</text>
  <text x="380" y="354" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Reed&#8211;Solomon means: send many evaluations of the message polynomial.</text>
</svg>
